.TH VEX-TIMER 1 "2026-11-24" "vex-timer 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vex-timer \- a command-line study timer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vex-timer
.B \-s
.I sessions
.B \-t
.I focus-minutes
.B \-b
.I break-minutes
.RB [ \-l
.IR long\-break\-minutes ]
.RB [ \-r
.IR every ]
.RB [ \-a
.IR alarm ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-notify ]
.br
.B vex-timer \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B vex-timer \-v | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vex-timer
schedules focus sessions and breaks, draws a live progress display, and plays
a synthesized chiptune alarm when a phase ends.
.PP
Each phase is driven by an absolute deadline using
.BR clock_gettime (2) " (" CLOCK_MONOTONIC ),
so delayed renders or interrupted sleeps do not make the countdown drift.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " sessions" | \-\-sessions= N
Number of study sessions, from 1 to 255. Required.
.TP
.BI \-t " focus-minutes" | \-\-focus= N
Focus duration in minutes, from 1 to 255. Required.
.TP
.BI \-b " break-minutes" | \-\-break= N
Break duration in minutes, from 1 to 255. Required.
.TP
.BI \-l " long-break-minutes" | \-\-long\-break= N
Long break duration in minutes, from 1 to 255. Optional; when omitted, no
long breaks run.
.TP
.BI \-r " every" | \-\-long\-break\-every= N
Take a long break after every N sessions, from 1 to 255 (default 4).
Requires \fB\-l\fR. Long breaks run between sessions only, never after the
final one.
.TP
.BI \-a " alarm" | \-\-alarm= NAME
Alarm sound (default: \fBmegalovania\fR). See \fBALARM SOUNDS\fR below.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-notify
Disable desktop notifications. Notifications are only sent when
.BR notify\-send (1)
is installed; otherwise every notification is a silent no-op.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit. The \fB\-\-help=value\fR form is rejected.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.PP
Long options also accept the \fB\-\-name=value\fR form, for example
\fB\-\-focus=25\fR or \fB\-\-alarm=tetris\fR. Values are whole minutes only;
signs, decimals, and trailing garbage are rejected.
.SH CONTROLS
Controls require an interactive terminal. When stdin is redirected the timer
still runs, but keyboard controls are unavailable and phase alarms use the
terminal bell.
.TP
.B "Space or P"
Pause or resume the current phase.
.TP
.B S
Skip the current phase. The phase is counted as completed.
.TP
.B Q
Quit immediately with exit status 130.
.TP
.B "Any key"
Stop a ringing alarm or the finish fanfare.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Quit immediately with exit status 130.
.SH "ALARM SOUNDS"
megalovania (default), remix, jazz, call-response, pvz, tetris, mario,
imperial, addictive, beep, hard-to-say-goodbye, cinematic, garden-guardian,
final-showdown, victory, none (silent; also skips the finish fanfare).
Audio playback pipes 16-bit mono 44.1 kHz samples to
.BR aplay (1)
and is Linux-only; when
.B aplay
is unavailable the timer falls back to the terminal bell.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value (regardless of its content), colors are
disabled in the live display. Colors are also disabled automatically when
stdout is not a terminal or \fBTERM\fR is \fBdumb\fR. See
.UR https://no-color.org/
.UE .
.TP
.B TERM
A value of \fBdumb\fR disables colors in the live display.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed successfully, or \fB\-\-help\fR / \fB\-\-version\fR was used.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments or configuration.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl+C or Q.
.TP
.BR "128 + signal"
Terminated by another handled signal, for example 143 for SIGTERM.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "vex-timer \-s 4 \-t 25 \-b 5"
Four 25-minute focus sessions with 5-minute breaks.
.TP
.B "vex-timer \-s 8 \-t 25 \-b 5 \-l 15 \-r 4"
Classic Pomodoro: a 15-minute break after every fourth session.
.TP
.B "vex-timer \-\-sessions=8 \-\-focus=25 \-\-break=5 \-\-alarm=tetris"
The \fB\-\-name=value\fR form with the Tetris theme as the alarm.
.TP
.B "vex-timer \-s 1 \-t 50 \-b 1 \-a none \-\-no\-notify"
A single 50-minute focus session with no sound or notifications.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aplay (1),
.BR notify\-send (1)
